hadiths[66]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1080","Abu Ayyub narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""Four are from the Sunan of the Messengers: Al-Hayat"
"1081","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:""We went with Allah's Messenger, while we were young men who had nothing. He said: 'O young men! You should marry, for indeed it helps in lowering the gaze and protecting the private parts. Whoever among you is not able to marry, then let him fast, for indeed fasting will diminish his sexual desire."""
"1082","Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab narrated from Sa'b bin Abi Waqqas:""The Messenger of Allah refused Uthman bin Ma'zun (when he asked) regarding celibacy"
"1083","""We went with Allah's Messenger, while we were young men who had nothing. He said: 'O young men! You should marry, for indeed it helps in lowering the gaze and protecting the private parts. Whoever among you is not able to marry, then let him fast, for indeed fasting will diminish his sexual desire."""
"1084","Abu Hatim Al-Muzani narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""When someone whose religion and character you are pleased with comes to you then marry (her to) him. If you do not do so"
"1085","""The Messenger of Allah refused Uthman bin Ma'zun (when he asked) regarding celibacy, and if he had permitted it for him, then we would have castrated ourselves."""
"1086","The Messenger of Allah said: ""When someone whose religion and character you are pleased with proposes to (someone under the care) of one of you, then marry to him. If you do not do so, then there will be turmoil (Fitnah) in the land and abounding discord (Fasad)."""
"1087","The Messenger of Allah said: ""When someone whose religion and character you are pleased with comes to you then marry (her to) him. If you do not do so, then there will be turmoil (Fitnah) in the land and discord (Fasad). If you do not do so, then there will be turmoil (Fitnah) in the land and discord (Fasad)."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What if there was something about him?""
He said: ""When someone whose religion and character you are pleased with comes to you then marry him."" (And he (pbuh) said this) three times."
"1088","The Prophet said: ""Indeed the woman is married for her religion, her wealth, and her beauty, so take the one with religion, and may your hands be dusty."""
"1089","Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah proposed to a woman, so the Prophet said: ""Look at her, for indeed that is more likely to make things better between the two of you."""
"1090","The Messenger of Allah said: ""The distinction between the lawful and the unlawful  is the Duff and the voice."""
"1091","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Publicize this marriage, and hold it in the Masjid, and beat the Duff for it."""
"1092","""The morning after the consummation of my marriage, the Prophet came and sat on my bed as far from me as you are sitting now, and our little girls started beating the Duff and reciting verses mourning my father who had been killed in the battle of Badr. One of them said: 'Among us is a Prophet who knows what will happen tomorrow.' On that the Prophet said: 'Stop saying this, and keep on saying what you were saying before.'"""
"1093","Anas bin Malik narrated:The Messenger of Allah saw some traces of saffron on `Abdur-Rahman bin `Awf so he said: 'What is this?' He said: 'I married a woman for the amount of gold equal to a date stone.' So he said: 'May Allah bless you. Have a banquet"
"1094","The Messenger of Allah said: ""If anyone of you, when having sexual intercourse with his wife, says: (Bismillah, Allahumma jannibnash-Shaitana wa jannibish-Shaitana ma razaqtana) 'In the Name of Allah, O Allah! Protect me from Shaitan and protect what you bestow upon us from Shaitan' - then if Allah decrees that they should have a child, Shaitan will not be able to harm him.'"""
"1095","(Another chain similar to the narration as no. 1095) :Others have reported this Hadith from Ibn Uyainah"
"1096","The Messenger of Allah saw some traces of saffron on `Abdur-Rahman bin `Awf so he said: 'What is this?' He said: 'I married a woman for the amount of gold equal to a date stone.' So he said: 'May Allah bless you. Have a banquet, even if with only one sheep.'"""
"1097","Ibn Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Accept the invitation when you are offered"
"1098","Others have reported this Hadith from Ibn Uyainah, from Az-Zuhri, from Anas, and they did not mention ""from Wa'il, from his son Nawf"" in it."
"1099","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Having food on the first day is was is obligatory, and having food on the second day is Sunnah, and having food on the third day is to be heard of, and whoever wants to be heard of, Allah will make him heard of."""
"1100","Abu Musa narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no marriage except with a Wali"
"1101","""A man named Abu Shu'aib came to a slave of his, who was a butcher, and said: 'Prepare some food for me that will be sufficient for five, for I have seen hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah.' So he prepared some food. Then he sent a message to the Prophet inviting him and those who were sitting with him. When the Prophet stood, he was followed by a man who was not with them when they were invited. When the Messenger of Allah arrive at the door he said to the owner of the house: 'A man who was not with us when you invited us followed us, if you permit him, he will enter.'"" He said: We have permitted him, let him enter."""
"1102","""I married a woman and went to the Prophet, he said: 'O Jabir! Have you married?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'A virgin or a matron?' I said: 'A matron.' He said: 'Why didn't you marry a young girl, so that you may play with her and she with you?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Abdullah (his father) died and left behind seven - or nine - daughter, so I have brought someone who can look after them.'"" (He said:) ""So he supplicated for me."""
"1103","Narrated by Ali ibn Hujr, who reported from Sharik ibn Abdullah, from Abu Ishaq — and also narrated by Qutaybah, who reported from Abu Awana, from Abu Ishaq — and also narrated by Muhammad ibn Bashshar, who reported from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq — and also narrated by Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad, who reported from Zayd ibn Hubab, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:

The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **""There is no marriage without a guardian (wali).""**

It is also narrated in this chapter from Aisha, Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayrah, Imran ibn Husayn, and Anas (may Allah be pleased with them all)."
"1104","Narrated Aisha: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whatever woman is married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void, her marriage is void, her marriage is void. If he has consummated the marriage with her, then she is entitled to a bridal-money for what he enjoyed of her private parts. And if they dispute, then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian.""

Abu Eisa said: This Hadith is Hasan. Yahya bin Sa'eed Al-Ansari, Yahya bin Ayyub, Sufyan Ath-Thawri, and more than one of the memorizers have narrated something similar to this from Ibn Juraij.

Abu Eisa said: The Hadith of Abu Musa is a Hadith about which there is disagreement. Israel, Shareek bin Abdullah, Abu Awanah, Zuhair bin Mu'awiyah, and Qais bin Ar-Rabi' narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (ﷺ). And Asbat bin Muhammad and Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated it from Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (ﷺ). And Abu Ubaidah Al-Haddad narrated it from Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (ﷺ) similarly, but he did not mention ""from Abu Ishaq"" in it. And it has also been narrated from Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from the Prophet (ﷺ). And Shu'bah and Ath-Thawri narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from the Prophet (ﷺ): ""There is no marriage except with a guardian."" Some of the companions of Sufyan have mentioned, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa - but this is not correct. The narration of those who narrated from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (ﷺ): ""There is no marriage except with a guardian"" is, in my view, more correct, because their hearing from Abu Ishaq was at different times. And even though Shu'bah and Ath-Thawri are more precise and reliable memorizers than all of those who narrated this Hadith from Abu Ishaq, the narration of these others is, in my view, more likely to be correct, because Shu'bah and Ath-Thawri heard this Hadith from Abu Ishaq in a single sitting. Among what indicates this is what Mahmoud bin Ghailan narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, he said: ""I heard Sufyan Ath-Thawri asking Abu Ishaq: 'Did you hear Abu Burdah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no marriage except with a guardian""?' He said: 'Yes.'"" This indicates that the hearing of this Hadith by Shu'bah and Ath-Thawri was at one time. And Israel is trustworthy and reliable regarding Abu Ishaq. I heard Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna saying: I heard Abdur-Rahman bin Mahdi saying: ""Whatever I missed of the Hadith of Ath-Thawri from Abu Ishaq, I only missed it because I relied on Israel, for he used to bring it more complete.""

And the Hadith of Aisha on this topic from the Prophet (ﷺ): ""There is no marriage except with a guardian"" is, in my view, a Hasan Hadith. It was narrated by Ibn Juraij, from Sulaiman bin Musa, from Az-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, from the Prophet (ﷺ). And it was narrated by Al-Hajjaj bin Artah and Ja'far bin Rabi'ah, from Az-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, from the Prophet (ﷺ). And it was narrated from Hisham bin Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, from the Prophet (ﷺ) similarly. Some of the people of Hadith have criticized the Hadith of Az-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, from the Prophet (ﷺ). Ibn Juraij said: ""Then I met Az-Zuhri and asked him about it, and he denied it."" So they weakened this Hadith because of this. And it was mentioned from Yahya bin Ma'in that he said: ""No one mentioned this wording from Ibn Juraij except Isma'il bin Ibrahim."" Yahya bin Ma'in said: ""And the hearing of Isma'il bin Ibrahim from Ibn Juraij is not up to that standard; he only verified his books against the books of Abdul-Majid bin Abdul-Aziz bin Abi Rawwad, what he heard from Ibn Juraij."" And Yahya weakened the narration of Isma'il bin Ibrahim from Ibn Juraij.

And the practice regarding this topic, according to the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), is based on the Hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ): ""There is no marriage except with a guardian."" Among them are Umar bin Al-Khattab, Ali bin Abi Talib, Abdullah bin Abbas, Abu Hurairah, and others. And it has been narrated similarly from some of the jurists among the Followers, that they said: ""There is no marriage except with a guardian."" Among them are Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab, Al-Hasan Al-Basri, Shuraih, Ibrahim An-Nakha'i, Umar bin Abdul-Aziz, and others. And this is the view of Sufyan Ath-Thawri, Al-Awza'i, Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, Malik, Ash-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq."
"1105","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Every Khutbah that does not have the Tashah-hud in it"
"1106","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""A matron should not be given in marriage until she is consulted"
"1107","""The Messenger of Allah taught us the Tashah-hud for Salat and the Tashah-hud for Al-Hajjah."" He said: ""The Tashah-hud for Salat is: (At-Tahiyyatulilah, was-walawtu wat-tayyibatu. As-Salamu alaika ayyuhan-Nabiyyu wa rahmatullilahi wa barakatuhu, As-Salamu alina wa ala ibadillahis-salihin. Ashahadu an la ilaha illallah, wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan abduha wa Raduluh.) 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and His blessings. Peace be upon us and all of the righteous worshippers of Allah. I testify that none has the right to be worshiped but Allah. and I testify that Muhammad is His slave and His Messenger.""And the Tashah-hud for Al-Hajjah is: 'Indeed all praise is due to Allah, we seek His aid, and we seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge with Allah from the evils of our souls and the mischief of our deeds. (Innal-Hamdlillahi nasta'inuhu, wa nastaghfirhu, wa na'udhu billahi min sharuri anfusina, wa sayy'ita a'malina, man yahdihi, sala mudilla lahu, wa manyudlil, fala Hadiya lahu, wa ashadu an la ilaha illallah wa ashadu anna Muhammadan abduhu wa Rasuluh) 'Whoever He guides - meaning Allah - then here is none to lead him astray, and whomever He misleads, then there is no guide for him. I testify that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is His worshipper and Messenger.'""
He said: ""And he recited three Ayat."""
"1108","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""An orphan is to be consulted about herself"
"1109","The Prophet said: ""A matron should not be given in marriage until she is consulted, and a virgin should not be given in marriage until her permission is sought, and her silence is her permission."""
"1110","The Messenger of Allah said: ""The matron has more right to herself than her Wali, and the virgin is to give permission for herself, and her silence is her permission."""
"1111","The Messenger of Allah said: ""An orphan is to be consulted about herself, then if she is silent that is her permission, and if she refuses, then do not authorize it (the marriage) for her"" (meaning: when she attains the age of puberty and refuses it.)"
"1112","Abdullah bin Amr bin Rabi'ah narrated from his father:""A woman from Banu Fazarah was married for (the dowry of) two sandals. So the Messenger of Allah said to her: 'Do you approve of (exchanging) yourself and your wealth for two sandals?' She said: 'Yes.'"" He said: ""So he permitted it"
"1113","Sahl bin Sa'd As-Sa'idi narrated that:A woman came to the Messenger of Allah and said: ""I present myself to you (for marriage)."" So she stood for a long time. Then a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Marry her to me if you have no need of her."" So he said: ""Do you have anything to give her as a dowry?"" He said: ""I have nothing except this Izar."" So the Messenger of Allah said: ""If you give her your Izar then you will have no Izar"
"1114","Abu Ayyub narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""Four are from the Sunan of the Messengers: Al-Hayat"
"1115","Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah said:""Three will receive their reward twice: A slave who fulfills the rights of Allah and the rights of his owners"
"1116","# Hadith of Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him)

**Narrated by al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, who narrated to us: Ishaq ibn 'Isa and 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh, who both said: Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him), that:**

A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""I have offered myself to you."" She stood for a long while. Then a man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, marry her to me if you have no need for her."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""Do you have anything that you could give her as a dowry (sadaq)?""** He replied, ""I have nothing but this izar (lower garment) of mine."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""If you give her your izar, you will sit without an izar. Seek something else.""** He said, ""I cannot find anything."" He ﷺ said, **""Seek something, even if it be a ring of iron.""** He sought but found nothing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""Do you have any portion of the Qur'an with you?""** He replied, ""Yes, such-and-such a surah and such-and-such a surah"" — naming certain surahs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""I have married her to you with what you have of the Qur'an.""**

---

**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** This is a *hasan sahih* hadith.

**Imam al-Shafi'i** (may Allah have mercy upon him) acted upon this hadith, stating: If a man has nothing to give as a dowry and marries a woman upon a surah of the Qur'an, the marriage is valid, and he should teach her a surah of the Qur'an.

**Some of the scholars of knowledge** said: The marriage is valid, and he should give her a dowry equivalent to her *mahr al-mithl* (customary dowry of her like). This is the position of the people of Kufah, **Ahmad**, and **Ishaq**.

---

*Related: Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, Sunan al-Tirmidhi, Kitab al-Nikah.*"
"1117","""Umar bin Al-Khattab said: 'Do not exaggerate in the dowries of women. If doing so was honorable in the world or Taqwa before Allah then Allah's Prophet would have been the first of you to do it. I do not know of the Messenger of Allah marrying any of his women, nor giving any of his daughters in marriage, for more than twelve Uqiyah."""
"1118","Jabir bin Abdullah and Ali narrated:""The Messenger of Allah cursed the Muhill and the one the Muhallal was done for"
"1119","""Three will receive their reward twice: A slave who fulfills the rights of Allah and the rights of his owners, then he will be given his reward twice. And a man who has a beautiful slave girl, so he teaches her good manners, then he frees her, then he married her seeking the Face of Allah by that; then he will be given his reward twice. And a man who believed in an earlier Book, then another Book came to him and he believed in it; then he will be given his reward twice."""
"1120","The Prophet said: ""Whichever man married a woman and entered into her, then it is not lawful for him to marry her daughter. If he did not enter into her then he may marry her daughter. And whichever man married a woman and he entered into her, or he did  not enter into her, then it is not lawful for him to marry her mother."""
"1121","Muhammad bin Ka'b narrated that:Ibn Abbas said: ""Mut'ah was only during the beginning of Islam. A man would arrive in a land that he was not familiar with so he would marry a woman for the extent of time that he thought he would remain there. So his Mut'ah was upheld and his case was fine until the (following) Ayah was revealed: Except their wives or what their right hands possess. Then every private part other than those became unlawful"
"1122","Imran bin Husain narrated that :The Prophet said: ""There is no Jalab"
"1123","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by 'Abdullāh ibn Mas'ūd (may Allāh be pleased with him):**

He said: ""The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed the one who performs a marriage solely for the purpose of making a woman lawful (*al-muḥill*) and the one for whom she is made lawful (*al-muḥallal lahu*).""

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith. And Abū Qays al-Awdī's name is 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Tharwān. This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) through other chains of narration. The practice (*al-'amal*) according to the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) — including 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, 'Uthmān ibn 'Affān, 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar, and others — is based upon this hadith. It is also the position of the jurists among the *Tābi'ūn*, and it is the view held by Sufyān al-Thawrī, Ibn al-Mubārak, al-Shāfi'ī, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq.""

He further said: ""I heard al-Jārūd ibn Mu'adh narrate from Wakī' that he held this view and said: 'The proponents of *ra'y* (personal opinion) should be condemned for their stance on this issue.' Al-Jārūd said: Wakī' also reported that Sufyān (al-Thawrī) said: 'If a man marries a woman solely to make her lawful for her former husband, and then it occurs to him to keep her, it is not permissible for him to retain her unless he marries her with a fresh, new marriage contract (*nikāḥ jadīd*).'""

---

**Note:** This hadith addresses the prohibition of *taḥlīl* marriage — a marriage contracted with the premeditated intention of divorcing the woman so that she may lawfully return to her former husband after a triple divorce (*ṭalāq*). Both the man who enters such a contract (*muḥill*) and the former husband who arranges it (*muḥallal lahu*) are subject to the curse (*la'nah*) of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1124","Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet prohibited marrying a woman along with her paternal aunt or along with her maternal aunt"
"1125","Ibn Abbas said: ""Mut'ah was only during the beginning of Islam. A man would arrive in a land that he was not familiar with so he would marry a woman for the extent of time that he thought he would remain there. So his Mut'ah was upheld and his case was fine until the (following) Ayah was revealed: Except their wives or what their right hands possess. Then every private part other than those became unlawful."""
"1126","Uqbah bin Amir Al-Juhani narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Indeed the conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those that make the private parts lawful among you"
"1127","Ibn Umar narrated:""Ghilan bin Salamah Ath-Thaqafi accepted Islam and he had ten wives in Jahiliyyah who accepted Islam along with him. So the Prophet ordered (him) to chose four (of them)"
"1128","Abu Wahb Al-Jaishani narrated that:He heard Ibn Fairuz Ad-Dhailami narrating from his father: ""I went to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I accepted Islam and I had two sisters (as wives).' So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Chose whichever of them you will"
"1129","""The Messenger of Allah prohibited that a woman be married along with her paternal aunt, or the paternal aunt along with her brother's daughter, or a woman with her maternal aunt, or the maternal aunt along with her sister's daughter, and the younger is not to be married with the older, nor the older with the younger."""
"1130","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Indeed the conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those that make the private parts lawful among you."""
"1131","""Ghilan bin Salamah Ath-Thaqafi accepted Islam and he had ten wives in Jahiliyyah who accepted Islam along with him. So the Prophet ordered (him) to chose four (of them)."""
"1132","He heard Ibn Fairuz Ad-Dhailami narrating from his father: ""I went to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I accepted Islam and I had two sisters (as wives).' So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Chose whichever of them you will.'"""
"1133","""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I accepted Islam and I had two sisters (as wives).' So Messenger of Allah said: 'Chose whichever of them you will.'""]"
"1134","Abu Bakr bin Al-Jahm narrated:""Abu Salamah bin Abdur-Rahman and I visited Fatimah bint Qais. She narrated to us that her husband had divorced her three times"
"1135","""We got some captives on the day of Awtas, and they had husbands among their peopled. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, so the following was revealed: And women who are already married, except those whom your right hands posses."
"1136","""The Messenger of Allah prohibited the price of a dog, the dowry of a fornicator, and the payment made to the fortune-teller."""
"1137","Abu Sa'eed narrated:""Azl was mentined before the Messenger of Allah and he said: 'Why would one of you do that?"
"1138","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān**, who said: **Abū Dāwūd** narrated to us, who said: **Shuʿbah** informed us, who said: **Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm** informed me, who said:

I and **Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān** entered upon **Fāṭimah bint Qays**, and she narrated to us that her husband had divorced her with a triple *ṭalāq* (irrevocable divorce) and had not assigned for her any lodging (*suknā*) nor maintenance (*nafaqah*).

She said: ""And he placed with a paternal cousin of his ten *aqfizah* for me — five of barley and five of wheat.""

She said: ""So I came to the **Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him**, and I mentioned that to him.""

She said: ""So he said: **'He has spoken the truth.'**""

She said: ""Then he commanded me to observe my *ʿiddah* (waiting period) in the house of **Umm Sharīk**. Then the **Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him**, said to me: **'Indeed, the house of Umm Sharīk is a house frequented by the Muhājirūn (Emigrants). Rather, observe your ʿiddah in the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm, for perhaps you may cast aside your garments and he will not see you. And when your ʿiddah has expired and someone comes seeking your hand in marriage, then inform me.'**""

She said: ""When my ʿiddah had expired, **Abū Jahm** and **Muʿāwiyah** proposed to me.""

She said: ""So I came to the **Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him**, and I mentioned that to him. He said: **'As for Muʿāwiyah, he is a man who possesses no wealth; and as for Abū Jahm, he is a man who is harsh with women.'**""

She said: ""Then **Usāmah ibn Zayd** proposed to me, and I married him. And **Allah blessed me through Usāmah.**""

---

**This is a *ṣaḥīḥ* (authentic) hadith.**

It was also narrated by **Sufyān al-Thawrī** from **Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm**, in a narration similar to this hadith, and he added therein that the **Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him**, said to her: **""Marry Usāmah.""**

**Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān**, who said: **Wakīʿ** narrated to us from **Sufyān**, from **Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm**, with this (chain and text)."
"1139","Aishah narrated that:The Prophet would divide (his time) equally between his wives and said: ""O Allah! This is my division in what I have control over"
"1140","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""When a man has two wives and he is not just between them"
"1141","Narrated to us by Ibn Abi 'Umar and Qutaybah, who both said: narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Qaz'ah ibn Yahya, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:

The practice of *'azl* (coitus interruptus) was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: **""Why would one of you do that?""**

Ibn Abi 'Umar added in his narration: **""Let none of you do that.""**

Both narrators stated in their version: **""Indeed, there is no soul that is created, except that Allah is its Creator.""**

He (the narrator) said: In this chapter, there is also a narration from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him).

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Abu Sa'id is a *hasan sahith* (good and authentic) hadith. It has been narrated through multiple chains from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him). A group of scholars among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and others considered *'azl* to be disliked (*makruh*)."
"1142","He (Abu Qilabah) said: ""If I wish, I could say: 'The Messenger of Allah said'"" but he said: ""The Sunnah when a man married a virgin after he already has a wife, is that he stays with her seven (nights). And when he married a matron when he already has a wife, he stays with her three (nights)."""
"1143","The Prophet would divide (his time) equally between his wives and said: ""O Allah! This is my division in what I have control over, so do not punish me for what You have control over which I do not have control over."""
"1144","Alqamah narrated that :Ibn Mas'ud was asked about a man who married a woman and he did not stipulate the dowry for her"
"1145","Ali (bin Abi Talib) narrated that The Messenger of Allah said:“Indeed Allah has made unlawful through suckling whatever He made unlawful through lineage.”"
